steps.detail:
Compressions get shallow when you tire, often without you noticing. If anyone else can help, swap about every 2 minutes (about 5 cycles of 30:2). Keep the pause for the swap as short as possible. The coach prompts swaps.

Keep going until:
- the person shows an obvious sign of life, such as breathing normally or moving;
- an AED is ready to use (then follow its prompts);
- another trained person takes over;
- medical help arrives and takes over;
- you are alone and too exhausted to continue;
- the scene becomes unsafe.
